    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nCurrently to achieve vim-surround keymaps in mini.surround, user has to do a bit of boiler plate.\nLike:\n```lua\nrequire('mini.surround').setup{\n    mappings = {\n      add = 'ys',\n      delete = 'ds',\n      find = '',\n      find_left = '',\n      highlight = '',\n      replace = 'cs',\n  }\n}\nvim.keymap.del('x', 'ys')\nvim.keymap.set('x', 'S', [[:<C-u>lua MiniSurround.add('visual')<CR>]], { silent = true })\nvim.keymap.set('n', 'yss', 'ys_', { remap = true }) -- Make special mapping for \"add surrounding for line\"\n```\nWhile this is nicely documented in help files , it would be really convenient to have a single field do all these.\n```lua\nrequire('mini.surround').setup{\n  preset= \"vim-surround\"\n}\n```\n\n",
